  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Activity under preparation FEASIBILITY STUDIES FOR THE REHABILITATION OF THE KENEMA &#xbf; BLAMA &#xbf; POTORU AND KENEMA &#xbf; JORU - TANINAHUN ROADS</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&lt;p&gt;The project forms part of the Government of Sierra Leone&apos;s strategic road infrastructure development programme to improve regional connectivity, reduce transport costs, and expand access to economic and social opportunities. It will support the preparation and updating of feasibility studies, detailed engineering designs, and tender documentation for priority road corridors in accordance with European Union (EU) and European Investment Bank (EIB) standards.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The assignment includes updating the feasibility study for the Kenema&#xbf;Joru&#xbf;Taninahun Road (Kenema&#xbf;Blama section) and preparing a new feasibility study for the upgrading of the Kenema&#xbf;Blama Road and reconstruction of the Blama&#xbf;Potoru Road. The studies will incorporate updated traffic forecasts, engineering standards, climate resilience, road safety, and environmental and social safeguards, including a Climate Risk and Vulnerability Assessment, Environmental and Social Impact Assessment (ESIA), and Environmental and Social Management Plan (ESMP).&lt;/p&gt;</narrative>
  </description>
